00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:00.540
So one of the things that
I want to just talk through is

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:04.440
how we have helped to
promote data science in the company.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:08.940
And so a lot of you are
probably leaders or you're

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:10.020
working in your companies,

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:14.280
trying to get momentum in terms
of making data science and

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:17.760
the power of data science
be more prominent in the company.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:21.000
And so when I joined Zoetis,
it was pretty early on.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.980
It was within the
first few months,

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.860
really noticing that there's
some data science groups that

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:27.660
exist, and we're bringing
in a data science team.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:30.240
We don't want there to
be confusion around, OK,

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:32.400
why are there so many
teams, who's doing what.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:35.700
We want to be more united,
be really a unified

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:41.160
one Zoetis team of data
scientists. So what we decided

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:45.360
to do was to create this
thing called the Zoetis data science forum

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:48.900
where we would meet
once a month and share

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:53.220
success stories with each
other, share use cases, share

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:56.100
code and best practices.

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:59.640
And so it started off with
roughly about 50 or so people

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.820
that would attend across all
of these different data science areas.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:05.640
And we met for several months,

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.020
we'd be sharing things
and it was great.

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:10.980
And then the tenants started to
build up a little bit more and

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:13.920
more and then more and more
non data scientists started to come

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:16.020
in and want to be interested
in what was going on.

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:18.960
And so it was at that
point we realized, well, wait a minute,

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:23.820
why don't we open up this to be
much more accessible to anyone in the company,

00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:26.760
not just have really kind
of technical kinds of topics,

00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:30.120
but talk more about the
business value and what's the

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.940
business impact. And have the
data science in there as well,

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:37.320
but have it be in a
very easy to understand manner and then

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:41.580
have that be a way of
promoting what great data science work is

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.280
across the company. So
as we started to do that,

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:46.500
more and more people started
to comment and enjoy it.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.360
And then

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:53.280
