really making sure that we're

00:43:53.460 --> 00:43:54.920
involving the right people.

00:43:54.920 --> 00:44:00.420
- So with all those various sources,

00:44:00.420 --> 00:44:04.020
these standardized on certain data
formats like you say like

00:44:04.020 --> 00:44:08.100
we'll accept CSV files,
JSON files, whatever.

00:44:08.660 --> 00:44:13.020
- Yeah, so within
Azure is our data lake.

00:44:13.020 --> 00:44:16.140
We've created data lake
within Azure. And honestly,

00:44:16.140 --> 00:44:17.940
how the data
engineers ingest it--

00:44:17.940 --> 00:44:20.160
I think it can come in
many different formats.

00:44:20.160 --> 00:44:22.260
We land it into a raw
zone. Then from there,

00:44:22.260 --> 00:44:24.780
it gets transformed,
put into parquet into

00:44:26.160 --> 00:44:27.900
our governance zone.
And from there,

00:44:27.900 --> 00:44:31.200
it can be consumed among
various downstream applications

00:44:31.200 --> 00:44:34.800
and consumers and
data scientists, et cetera.

00:44:34.800 --> 00:44:38.580
So yeah, a lot of different
ways. I think Javier has

