00:45:16.320 --> 00:45:20.580
it's the R integrations that

00:45:20.580 --> 00:45:25.080
might make the Power BI
dashboards faster. This is

00:45:25.080 --> 00:45:26.940
something, again, I
haven't researched at all.

00:45:26.940 --> 00:45:29.940
But I didn't know if
you're using any kind of

00:45:29.940 --> 00:45:32.580
R backend for

00:45:34.740 --> 00:45:36.300
powering the

00:45:36.300 --> 00:45:38.100
Power BI visuals.

00:45:38.100 --> 00:45:40.020
- Yeah, great question.

00:45:40.020 --> 00:45:42.780
Now I don't know of
any instances of that.

00:45:42.780 --> 00:45:44.580
The backend

00:45:44.580 --> 00:45:48.540
piece on the data for
our Power BI or from

00:45:49.920 --> 00:45:52.860
basically Azure-- so
we use Data Factory or

00:45:54.060 --> 00:45:57.240
SQL or something-- data
transformations, data storage,

00:45:57.240 --> 00:46:00.300
and then the RBI dashboards
are just built on top of that.

00:46:00.840 --> 00:46:04.320
And so we use R for-- the
way we think of it as--

00:46:04.320 --> 00:46:09.180
so the whole process of data
is they're source systems,

00:46:09.180 --> 00:46:12.480
then they get loaded into the
data lake in it's raw format,

00:46:12.480 --> 00:46:14.640
it's transformed, then it's
governed, and it becomes

00:46:15.180 --> 00:46:16.740
our data source.

00:46:16.740 --> 00:46:20.760
And I think of everything
that we do in data science as

00:46:20.760 --> 00:46:25.920
downstream of that curated
governed data. And so the apps

00:46:25.920 --> 00:46:31.200
that we build using Posit
are downstream of that production data.

00:46:31.740 --> 00:46:32.460
And

00:46:32.460 --> 00:46:36.480
the Power BI dashboards
are also downstream of that

00:46:36.480 --> 00:46:38.880
production data, but we don't
have Posit in the middle.

00:46:38.880 --> 00:46:42.420
So we don't necessarily
use Posit it as a

00:46:43.680 --> 00:46:47.760
data engineering platform to create
the data in its format.

00:46:50.580 --> 00:46:53.460
I think, in general,
we would prefer to have

00:46:53.460 --> 00:46:55.080
the data engineering

00:46:55.740 --> 00:46:58.440
steps be done within
kind of Azure,

00:46:58.440 --> 00:46:59.040
Data Factory,

00:47:00.480 --> 00:47:04.800
all the SQL and all that
the massaging curating of the data

00:47:04.800 --> 00:47:07.140
to happen there and have
the data ready for consumption

00:47:07.920 --> 00:47:08.760
downstream of that

00:47:10.200 --> 00:47:11.220
in general.

00:47:11.220 --> 00:47:12.900
JAVIER: No, that makes
